From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:55:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] DirectStorage: workers read a file through a handle each
 (VICTORY_DSTORAGE_HANDLES=0: one handle, as before)

The title's file handle is opened for synchronous reads, and the host
does the reads of one such handle one after the other: every worker read
an archive through one queue. Each worker now reads through a handle of
its own, made from the title's with ReOpenFile when the worker first
reads that file; the title's handle is read if the host gives no other.

Hand port of upstream pull request #2904 by 0xkn0wh3r3 (after avatarmanz,
fbc1830), which measured 185 -> 990 MB/s for 48 KiB random reads with 24
workers. On by default, as upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
